<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 3.057 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 3.057 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said the average yield at this week's auction of C$2.4 billion of 91-day Government of Canada treasury bills due July 10, 1997 was 3.057 percent, down from 3.278 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.3 billion of 182-day T-bills due October 9, 1997 was 3.479 percent, down from 3.630 percent last week, and on C$1.1 billion of 357-day T-bills due April 4, 1998 was 4.356 percent, up from 4.220 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$475 million three-month, C$125 million six-month and C$125 million one-year bills. It holds C$600 million of C$4.90 billion bills due April 17. (Details follow)  </p>
